  "title": "What does a zero determinant do to space?",
  "body": " What does a zero determinant do to space?   Suppose for a matrix . Forget the formula for a moment and think only about the picture: what does do to the whole plane? Why can no such map be undone?    The determinant is the area of the image of the unit square. If that area is zero, the square has been squashed flat. Where could every output vector possibly live?   "
