  "body": " The quadratic-form test   Let be symmetric, and let Let Then:     1.  is positive definite if and only if and .    2.  is negative definite if and only if and .    3.  is indefinite if .       Assume first that . Complete the square:   If and , then both coefficients are positive. The form is positive except at the origin.  If and , then both coefficients are negative. The form is negative except at the origin.  If and , then the two square terms have opposite signs. The form takes both positive and negative values, so it is indefinite.  If and , then so . In that case Taking , the expression takes both positive and negative values as varies. So is indefinite.   "
