  "body": " The origin has no preferred angle   The motion for all is perfectly still. Its velocity is But in polar coordinates this same motion can be written as or for , or with almost any other angle function. The angle does not describe anything real when .  So polar formulas must be used with care at the origin. A point at the origin has no well-defined radial direction and no well-defined angular direction.   "
