  "title": "Reading steepness and shape from contours?",
  "body": " Reading steepness and shape from contours?   You are handed a contour map you have never seen before, with no formula attached. From the picture alone, how would you decide where the surface is steepest, and how would the shape of a single level curve hint at which direction the function changes most slowly?    Spacing answers the first question and elongation answers the second. Ask yourself where the curves bunch up, and along which direction a single curve stretches out the farthest.   "
