  "title": "Why won’t the patches glue?",
  "body": " Why won’t the patches glue?   On every small patch, equals for an honest potential, so the curl test passes everywhere and local potentials genuinely exist. What goes wrong when you try to stitch all these local angle functions into one continuous potential on the whole punctured plane, and how does this story illustrate that the curl test is necessary but only sufficient once the domain is simply connected?    Follow once around the origin and watch its value when you return to the start. A single-valued function must come back to where it began—does the angle? The missing point is what prevents the loop from shrinking, and that is precisely the failure of simple connectivity.   "
