  "title": "Where could a hidden source hide?",
  "body": " Where could a hidden source hide?   The hypotheses ask to have continuous partial derivatives on an open region containing . If we quietly ignored a singularity or a jump inside , why might the interior integral of come out too small compared to the true boundary flux?    A place where the field is not smooth can act like an extra, unseen boundary. Ask yourself where flux could be entering or leaving that the integral over the smooth part of never gets to count.   "
