  "body": " The straight ramp minimizes energy   Let and consider Now perturb by a smooth function that vanishes on the boundary: The boundary values do not change, because on .  Compute the energy: The middle term is Integrate in : because is zero on the boundary.  Therefore The added term is always nonnegative. So the ramp has the smallest energy among these boundary-preserving perturbations.   "
